{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The report’s central inference is methodologically plausible: it uses all 54 participant COPEs, a positive one-sample test, and whole-brain max-T correction, while clearly describing uncertainty and the upstream scaling limit. The main reproducibility gap is that the code’s required Python packages and fetched atlas/mask resources have no worker-supplied environment declaration, so I’m recording replay as not checked rather than reconstructing dependencies."}}
