 The script checks participant identity, finite values, shared shape and affine, and common spatial support; it documents no exclusions, a fixed random seed, permutation count, and ROI definition. The atlas-based vmPFC label is an explicit localization aid, and the report appropriately limits claims given absent participant variance maps and the upstream gain scaling. The sign-flip result depends on symmetric participant-level errors under the null; the group result is conditional on the supplied first-level estimates. No independent replay was available to confirm the shipped result.\",\n      \"start_line\": 11,\n      \"end_line\": 11\n    }\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": {\n    \"quote\": \"Among the 54 participants in NARPS's equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** provide whole-brain family-wise corrected evidence for a gain-related increase in vmPFC.\",\n    \"start_line\": 13,\n    \"end_line\": 13\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
