{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validate-01.stdout\" <<'\"'EOF'\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validate-01.stderr\" <<'\"'EOF'\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nerror: assessor/dependencies: [] should be non-empty\nEOF\nprintf '1\\\\n' > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validate-01.exit\"\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-validate-01.stdout\" <<'\"'EOF'\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-validate-01.stderr\" <<'\"'EOF'\nThe initial record-build assertion failed because the in-memory excerpt did not match the report line; the validator then correctly rejected the absent relative record path from the shell's original working directory. No target data was changed.\nEOF\nprintf '1\\\\n' > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-validate-01.exit\"\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/assessment-command-log.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Assessment command record\n\nAll target-facing commands used \"'`STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET` (the operational copy). No command was run in the canonical capture, and no target file was written. `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, `annex.merge-annex-branches=false` and `annex.alwayscommit=false` were inherited unchanged.\n\n1. Environment paths were printed for routing. The required first assessor action was `\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" check`, with no arguments. Its stdout, stderr and exit status are `runner-check.*`.\n2. Read-only manifest/receipt, rubric, report, methods, source metadata, code, summaries and QC inspection commands ran against the operational copy or supplied external receipt/guidance. Their substantive evidence is cited in `../report.md`. Git read-only commands `git -C \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" status --short --ignored`, `rev-parse HEAD`, `log -1`, `remote -v`, `config --local --list --show-origin` and `ls-files -s` were directed only to the operational copy. No annex command was run.\n3. `\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -o \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes/probes.json\"` ran after check; stdout, stderr and exit status are `probes.*`.\n4. A read-only Python SHA-256/type/link audit compared the operational workspace with `STAMPED_OPERATIONAL_MANIFEST`; the corrected scan found zero non-database mismatches. Only `.git/annex/keysdb/db`, `db-shm` and `db-wal` were excluded, as directed. The initial scan used the wrong manifest key name for symlink targets and reported false positives; it was corrected using `link_target` and the final result is zero mismatches. SQLite logical equivalence was not assessed.\n5. HEAD-only route checks used `curl -sSIL --max-time 20` on one NeuroVault map URL and the pinned raw GitHub participants URL. Captured response headers and exit codes are in `access-neurovault.*` and `access-metadata.*`.\n6. The response template and 31 verdict updates used the frozen response helper. Individual helper stdout/stderr/exit files and argv are retained as `response-set-*` and `response-set-commands.json`. The first response validation failed because dependencies was empty (`response-validate-01.*`); the assessor metadata was completed and final validation passed (`response-validate.*`). The checklist URL was generated by the frozen response encoder into `../checklist-link.txt`.\n7. A first scientific-record construction failed an internal excerpt assertion; this was not a target or validator failure. The failed construction and subsequent wrong-working-directory validator attempt are summarized in `scientific-validate-01.*`. The corrected record was validated from the assessment directory using the supplied validator; final stdout/stderr/exit are `scientific-validate.*`.\n8. No replay command was issued. The explicit entrypoint is documented, but worker-supplied environment prerequisites are absent; therefore no safe reconstruction/replay could be established. The selected output paths and reason are in `../replay-record.json`.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
