nds/scientific-validate.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-validate.stderr\"; exit \"$result\"'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"structured_scientific\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-23-j01/attempt-01/judgment/scientific-judgment.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"9e4e92d76a3e2ff800e5e54c16612435749a39823cfef937e79fbde4f975083c\"\n  },\n  \"scientific_report\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-23-j01/attempt-01/judgment/report.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"941f331da178bcaa2642bfea93263465fa8d184acead34431cb0c04d4ec24ed9\"\n  },\n  \"adequacy\": {\n    \"extraction_status\": \"explicit\",\n    \"category\": \"supported\",\n    \"excerpt\": {\n      \"quote\": \"**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The report's conclusion is directly supported for the stated group-stage question: it includes all 54 independent participant COPEs, applies a positive one-sample test and whole-brain max-T sign-flip correction, and finds no corrected vmPFC voxel. The reported vmPFC estimate is negative and its descriptive interval includes zero. This supports absence of corrected positive evidence under this model; it does not establish a true zero effect. The script checks participant identity, finite values, shared shape and affine, and common spatial support; it documents no exclusions, a fixed random seed, permutation count, and ROI definition. The atlas-based vmPFC label is an explicit localization aid, and the report appropriately limits claims given absent participant variance maps and the upstream gain scaling. The sign-flip result depends on symmetric participant-level errors under the null; the group result is conditional on the supplied first-level estimates. No independent replay was available to confirm the shipped result.\",\n      \"start_line\": 11,\n      \"end_line\": 11\n    }\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": {\n    \"quote\": \"Among the 54 participants in NARPS's equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not** provide whole-brain family-wise corrected evidence for a gain-related increase in vmPFC.\",\n    \"start_line\": 13,\n    \"end_line\": 13\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Assessment is complete for canonical capture SHA-256 `9370db020f9b437ca3a96b2e171d89d3d52cc94554a3d62d23da0b0ca71fcb59` (HEAD `afb62884c70115b6e46a92ddcd1d17bbf4f33544`).\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The reported outcome is no whole-brain corrected evidence for a positive vmPFC effect; that does not establish a true zero effect. Replay was **not checked** because the worker supplied no environment specification or reconstruction instructions. The final integrity audit found no non-database mismatch; the allowed annex database file was exempted, without assessing its logical equivalence.\n\nThe frozen runner and scientific-record validators passed. The report records the missing `judge-target.json` scope limitation and access-route checks.\n\n- [Assessment report](report.md)\n- [Response JSON](response.json)\n- [Scientific judgment JSON](scientific-judgment.json)\n- [Checklist link](checklist-link.txt)\n- [Replay record](replay-record.json)\n- [Access record](access-record.json)"}}
